            {'p': 'OSINT (open-source intelligence) is the collection and analysis of information from sources that are open to the public. For business it is already a working tool: checking partners, preparing for negotiations, reading a market, assessing reputational risk and looking for assets all rest largely on open data.'},
            {'p': 'The main advantage is legality. The information comes from sources that do not need a special permit. The volume is huge, though, and the value is not the search itself but the ability to select what is relevant, check it and interpret it correctly.'},
