            {'h': 'From data to conclusions', 'p': 'Raw data rarely gives a ready answer. An analyst compares information from different sources, builds a chronology and a map of links between companies and people. That is where the patterns appear: repeated addresses, shared directors, changes of ownership that happen at the same time.'},
            {'h': 'Checking reliability', 'p': 'Open sources contain errors, outdated records and deliberate disinformation. Every important fact is therefore confirmed by at least two independent sources, and the final report separates established facts, assumptions and what remains uncertain.'},
